#
# rk3399-gru.dtsi includes cros-ec-keyboard.dtsi (google,cros-ec-keyb), which
# registers an input device named "cros_ec" even on Scarlet (a pure tablet with
# no physical matrix keyboard). Without a device-specific keylayout, EventHub
# falls back to Generic.kl, sees KEY_Q (key 16 -> AKEYCODE_Q), and classifies
# "cros_ec" as an external ALPHAKEY physical keyboard, suppressing the
# on-screen soft keyboard (IME).
#
# Map only non-alphabetic power/volume keys here so EventHub classifies
# "cros_ec" as KEYBOARD without ALPHAKEY.
#

key 114   VOLUME_DOWN
key 115   VOLUME_UP
key 116   POWER
